# No .gitattributes existed before, so checkouts followed whatever the
# user's own global core.autocrlf happened to be - on Windows (the only
# supported platform) that's commonly core.autocrlf=true, which converts
# every tracked text file to CRLF on checkout. Pinning eol=lf here instead
# makes checkouts consistent across machines regardless of that setting, so
# line endings alone can never make a freshly-pulled tracked file look
# locally modified.
* text=auto eol=lf
